<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Little Bighorn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1876">1876</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Custer's Last Stand · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-sioux-war-of-1876">Great Sioux War of 1876</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Little Bighorn was fought on 25–26 June 1876 near the Little Bighorn River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a>. Lakota, Northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a> and Arapaho warriors led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitting-bull">Sitting Bull</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crazy-horse">Crazy Horse</a> and others destroyed five companies of the US 7th Cavalry under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-armstrong-custer">George Armstrong Custer</a>, who was killed with all the men under his direct command. It was the greatest Native American victory of the Plains Wars, but it provoked a stronger US campaign that forced the Lakota onto reservations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-little-bighorn.jpg" alt="Battle of the Little Bighorn" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Marion Russell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Marion_Russell_-_The_Custer_Fight_(1903).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
